message: "If you use secondop-panel in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "secondop-panel"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/secondop-panel"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/secondop-panel"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A second opinion that is actually plural. A review request is fanned out to several model
  families at once, with a verdict contract, quorum counted by family rather than by head,
  and an exit code that refuses to go green when no real second opinion was obtained. An
  unknown rail is a visible skip, never a silent redirect into whichever vendor happens to
  work, because a verdict from vendor A printed under the name of vendor C makes the
  independence fake. Works with local CLIs, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or a mix.
  Includes a measured demonstration that a panel given file paths instead of file contents
  produces confident, professional and entirely fabricated findings.
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - code-review
  - multi-model
  - hallucination
  - quorum
  - ai-agents
